        "content": [
         {
          "attrs": {
           "accessLevel": "",
           "id": "6089a4c12a753d0071341edb",
           "localId": "e956bd13-1958-4e67-88be-ec7e93909a1a",
           "text": "@Jared Whiklo"
          },
          "type": "mention"
         },
         {
          "text": " just wanted to mention i’m not sure if it’s appropriate to make this change in a minor release, since it is taking away a “feature” even if its a buggy one. But I also don’t feel strongly about it and would personally rather have it resolved sooner rather than later. The more immediately addressable ticket would be ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "attrs": {
           "localId": "1a8a030a4cb3",
           "url": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-4096?src=confmacro"
          },
          "type": "inlineCard"
         },
         {
          "text": "  but its also not high value. That one and this one ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "attrs": {
           "localId": "d07923d27912",
           "url": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-4100?src=confmacro"
          },
          "type": "inlineCard"
         },
         {
          "text": "  were what i was thinking would be good to target for a 7.1.0 release, but we could consider all three if we are okay with blocking/ignoring a property in a minor release. My guess is (almost?) no one intentionally wants to add a second hasSize property to their binaries.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
