  "description": "<p>At present fedora supports setting premis:hasSize / premis3:size in an attempt to allow external binaries where fedora either cannot or should not retrieve the external content in order to determine the size of the file. This <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-4096\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">allowance is problematic and produces unexpected outcomes</a>. In fedora 4 it was server managed, but we changed it to being <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-2923\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">server generated with the option to set additional values in fedora 5</a>. Updating these properties does not actually affect Content-Size response headers in fedora 6 or 7.</p>\n\n<p>We should change both premis:hasSize and premis3:size to being server managed again. Those properties should be exclusively set from the fedora header file size property. We will need to decide whether a client sending a premis:hasSize/premis3:size property in an RDF body should be silently ignored, or rejected. </p>",
  "duedate": null,
